MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Geolocation::StartRequest 在任何权限检查之前就用伪装坐标应答并 return —— 弹窗不
出现，内容设置不被写。于是 permissions.query 仍报 'prompt'，而 getCurrentPosition()
一毫秒就拿到坐标。

这一对在原版 Chrome 里够不着：'prompt' 意味着用户还没决定，要成功拿到位置就必须
弹窗、等用户、最后停在 'granted'。所以报 'prompt' 不是「没伪装好」，是阳性的篡改
证据 —— 和当年 headless Chrome 那个经典破绽同一个形状（通知权限的声称与实际行为
对不上），站点两行 JS 就能读。

改在 GetOrCreatePermissionStatusListener：query、request、以及批量/verify 三条路径
全经过它，对已存在 listener 的 SetStatus 更新也覆盖到。granted 是对这个浏览器的
诚实描述 —— 它确实会无条件应答地理位置。

只在 geolocation 开关都非空时生效。实测：配了坐标 geo=granted / notif=prompt /
cam=prompt；没配坐标 geo=prompt 且调用失败。改动落在所有权限共用的收口上，所以
后两条不是锦上添花 —— 它们才是「只做该做的那件事」的证据。

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../modules/permissions/permissions.cc        | 29 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/permissions/permissions.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/permissions/permissions.cc
index e36c344035..23f79e6f53 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/permissions/permissions.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/permissions/permissions.cc
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/modules/permissions/permission_status.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/modules/permissions/permission_utils.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/bindings/exception_code.h"
+#include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fingerbrowser/fingerbrowser_fingerprint.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/wtf/functional.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/wtf/vector.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/wtf/wtf_size_t.h"
@@ -384,6 +385,34 @@ void Permissions::PermissionVerificationComplete(
 PermissionStatusListener* Permissions::GetOrCreatePermissionStatusListener(
     mojom::blink::PermissionStatusWithDetailsPtr status,
     mojom::blink::PermissionDescriptorPtr descriptor) {
+  // FingerBrowser: when this profile has a spoofed geolocation configured,
+  // Geolocation::StartRequest answers getCurrentPosition() from it and returns
+  // before any permission check runs -- no prompt is shown and the stored
+  // content setting is never touched. The setting therefore stays ASK, so this
+  // query reports "prompt" while the very next getCurrentPosition() call
+  // resolves with coordinates in about a millisecond.
+  //
+  // That pair is unreachable in stock Chrome: "prompt" means the user has not
+  // decided, so a successful position requires showing a prompt, waiting for
+  // the user, and ending up at "granted". Reporting "prompt" here is not a
+  // missing disguise, it is positive evidence of tampering -- and it is the
+  // same shape as the classic headless-Chrome tell, where Notification
+  // permission disagreed with what the API actually did. Two lines of script
+  // read it.
+  //
+  // "granted" is the honest description of what this browser will do: it
+  // answers geolocation unconditionally. This is the single point every path
+  // funnels through (query, request, and the bulk/verify path), and it also
+  // covers later SetStatus updates on an existing listener.
+  if (status && descriptor &&
+      descriptor->name == mojom::blink::PermissionName::GEOLOCATION &&
+      !fingerbrowser::SwitchValue(fingerbrowser::kGeoLatitudeE6Switch)
+           .empty() &&
+      !fingerbrowser::SwitchValue(fingerbrowser::kGeoLongitudeE6Switch)
+           .empty()) {
+    status->status = mojom::blink::PermissionStatus::GRANTED;
+  }
+
   auto type = GetPermissionType(*descriptor);
   if (!type)
     return nullptr;
